// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-03-17 | Modified: 2023-06-23
// ATT&CK: discovery, credential-access, T1040
// Description: Detects execution of PktMon, a tool that captures network packets.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Pktmon/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_pktmon_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\pktmon.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "PktMon.exe"
